# R23 Volunteers (side quest): Tamsin Ledger's militia roll. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ start
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: The militia must be enrolled in triplicate, or it is a mob. I need three named volunteers' signatures on this roll. Sergeant Gaunt, Mr Quill and Mr Pennywhistle have each said they would sign, and each has an objection.
give wv_signed_roll
set wv_vol_asked
quest vigil_volunteers asked
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what the objections are -> objections
* Ask what a lawful militia can do that a mob cannot -> lawful
* Take the roll and go -> END

~ objections
tamsin_ledger [weary]: The Sergeant wants the rear. Mr Quill wants his elegy entered as a regimental hymn. Mr Pennywhistle wants it noted that he is not a volunteer, he is a vendor. I have noted all three.
-> menu

~ lawful
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: A lawful militia can be ordered to hold a line. A mob can only be asked. I find it is the same people either way, and the paperwork is the difference.
-> menu

~ progress
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: The roll needs three signatures. I count them in the margin.
-> progress_menu

~ progress_menu
* [if flag.vol_signed >= 3] Hand in the signed roll -> file
* Ask which signatures are missing -> missing
* [if item:wv_last_letters and not flag.letter_tamsin] Hand Tamsin the letter from the county seat -> vigil/letters:to_tamsin
* [ends:vigil_volunteers] Tell her the roll cannot be filled -> refuse
* Leave -> END

~ missing
if not flag.vol_gaunt
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: The Sergeant has not signed. He is by the barricade, volunteering for the rear.
endif
if not flag.vol_quill
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Mr Quill has not signed. He is in the inn yard, composing.
endif
if not flag.vol_barnaby
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Mr Pennywhistle has not signed. He is selling something near the notice board.
endif
if flag.vol_signed >= 3
tamsin_ledger [smile]: All three have signed. Bring me the roll.
endif
-> progress_menu

~ file
tamsin_ledger [smile]: In triplicate. Stamped, and filed. The village has a lawful militia, and I must say it is a little startling how much better it feels.
take wv_signed_roll
quest vigil_volunteers filed
set vol_resolved
set wv_militia_lawful
temp_hp 2d8 party
-> END

~ refuse
tamsin_ledger [sad]: Then it is a mob. I will leave the roll blank. The barricade will be held by whoever is standing at it.
take wv_signed_roll
quest vigil_volunteers refused
set vol_resolved
-> END

~ after
if flag.wv_militia_lawful
tamsin_ledger [smile]: The militia is lawful. If the Wicker Man comes, it will have to file a complaint.
else
tamsin_ledger [weary]: The barricade will be held by whoever is standing at it. I have entered that as a finding.
endif
-> END

~ desk
Narrator: A trestle desk, a queue of volunteers, a quill that has been chewed on. The queue goes round the well and back to the desk, because Tamsin has asked everyone to enrol twice.
-> END

~ gaunt
sgt_gaunt [smile]: Sign the Ledger woman's roll? Gladly. I volunteer for the rear. Somebody has to watch it. I have never lost a battle I was present for the end of, and I mean to keep that record.
-> gaunt_menu

~ gaunt_menu
* [Persuasion DC 13] Tell him the rear is where the roll needs his name -> gaunt_sign | gaunt_stall
* [Intimidation DC 13] Tell him that the rear is also facing the Wicker Man -> gaunt_sign | gaunt_stall
* Offer him a posting: commander of the rear guard, in writing -> gaunt_rear
* Leave him to his post -> END

~ gaunt_sign
Narrator: He signs with a flourish, the way a man signs for something he plans never to deliver.
set vol_gaunt
set vol_signed += 1
-> END

~ gaunt_stall
sgt_gaunt [sad]: I would sign, I would, but my quill has gone dry. Perhaps later. When it is quieter.
-> gaunt_menu

~ gaunt_rear
Narrator: His chest rises. He writes REAR GUARD in letters twice the size of his name and signs under it.
set vol_gaunt
set vol_signed += 1
-> END
